			";s:7:"attribs";a:0:{}s:8:"xml_base";s:0:"";s:17:"xml_base_explicit";b:0;s:8:"xml_lang";s:0:"";s:5:"child";a:3:{s:0:"";a:6:{s:5:"title";a:1:{i:0;a:5:{s:4:"data";s:57:"Get Ready For LearnDash 5.0: How to Prepare Your Site Now";s:7:"attribs";a:0:{}s:8:"xml_base";s:0:"";s:17:"xml_base_explicit";b:0;s:8:"xml_lang";s:0:"";}}s:4:"link";a:1:{i:0;a:5:{s:4:"data";s:63:"https://www.learndash.com/blog/learndash-5-0-preparation-guide/";s:7:"attribs";a:0:{}s:8:"xml_base";s:0:"";s:17:"xml_base_explicit";b:0;s:8:"xml_lang";s:0:"";}}s:7:"pubDate";a:1:{i:0;a:5:{s:4:"data";s:31:"Mon, 20 Oct 2025 19:06:03 +0000";s:7:"attribs";a:0:{}s:8:"xml_base";s:0:"";s:17:"xml_base_explicit";b:0;s:8:"xml_lang";s:0:"";}}s:8:"category";a:1:{i:0;a:5:{s:4:"data";s:13:"Announcements";s:7:"attribs";a:0:{}s:8:"xml_base";s:0:"";s:17:"xml_base_explicit";b:0;s:8:"xml_lang";s:0:"";}}s:4:"guid";a:1:{i:0;a:5:{s:4:"data";s:34:"https://www.learndash.com/?p=27168";s:7:"attribs";a:1:{s:0:"";a:1:{s:11:"isPermaLink";s:5:"false";}}s:8:"xml_base";s:0:"";s:17:"xml_base_explicit";b:0;s:8:"xml_lang";s:0:"";}}s:11:"description";a:1:{i:0;a:5:{s:4:"data";s:261:"LearnDash 5.0 is coming—faster, smarter, and built for the future of online learning. This guide walks you through everything you need to do now to prepare your site, test with confidence, and unlock all the benefits of the new REST API and upcoming features.";s:7:"attribs";a:0:{}s:8:"xml_base";s:0:"";s:17:"xml_base_explicit";b:0;s:8:"xml_lang";s:0:"";}}}s:32:"http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/";a:1:{s:7:"creator";a:1:{i:0;a:5:{s:4:"data";s:9:"StellarWP";s:7:"attribs";a:0:{}s:8:"xml_base";s:0:"";s:17:"xml_base_explicit";b:0;s:8:"xml_lang";s:0:"";}}}s:40:"http://purl.org/rss/1.0/modules/content/";a:1:{s:7:"encoded";a:1:{i:0;a:5:{s:4:"data";s:21251:"
<div class="wp-block-group has-theme-palette-8-background-color has-background"><div class="wp-block-group__inner-container is-layout-constrained wp-block-group-is-layout-constrained">
<h2 class="kt-adv-heading27168_f72cd1-ab wp-block-kadence-advancedheading" data-kb-block="kb-adv-heading27168_f72cd1-ab">LearnDash 5.0 is now live!</h2>



<p class="has-text-align-center">After months of development and testing with our integration partners, <strong>LearnDash 5.0 is now available</strong>. <br>See what’s new — and how to get started — in this <a href="https://www.learndash.com/blog/learndash-5-0-is-live-your-lms-just-got-better/">release post</a>. </p>
</div></div>



<p>LearnDash 5.0 is just around the corner, and it’s one of the most important updates we’ve ever released.</p>



<p>This version introduces a modernized REST API, built to make LearnDash more reliable, scalable, and ready for the next generation of learning tools. It’s the foundation for everything coming next: a better user experience, smarter analytics, AI-assisted course creation, stronger integrations, and a reimagined Student Management experience.<br><br>We know big updates can feel overwhelming, but we’re taking every step necessary to ensure a smooth transition for our customers and our network of third-party developers and integration partners. That includes early developer access and coordinated testing with key partners.</p>



<p>To ensure your site is ready, we recommend taking a few proactive steps now and around the release. Preparing now means a smoother, more confident update with LearnDash 5.0 releases.</p>



<h2 class="wp-block-heading" id="h-what-to-expect-from-learndash-5-0-and-why-it-s-important-nbsp">What to Expect from LearnDash 5.0 and Why it’s Important&nbsp;</h2>



<p>LearnDash 5.0 is about future-proofing how LearnDash works at its core.</p>



<p>Our development team has made significant improvements to the LearnDash REST API, the system that powers how LearnDash shares data with add-ons, automations, and integrations.&nbsp;</p>



<p>This modernization:</p>



<ul class="wp-block-list">
<li>Makes LearnDash more stable and predictable</li>



<li>Improves site performance and scalability</li>



<li>Enables future AI integrations and more intelligent workflows</li>



<li>Opens the door for bug fixes blocked by legacy code<br></li>
</ul>



<p>In short: LearnDash 5.0 clears out years of technical debt and replaces it with a modern foundation designed to support the next decade of innovation.</p>



<h2 class="wp-block-heading" id="h-how-to-prepare">How to Prepare</h2>



<p>To help you get ready, we’ve broken this into two checklists:</p>



<ol class="wp-block-list">
<li><strong>Before LearnDash 5.0 Is Released</strong>:&nbsp; Steps you can take now to reduce risk and streamline your update.&nbsp;</li>



<li><strong>Before Updating to LearnDash 5.0</strong>: Checks to run right before installing the update.<br></li>
</ol>



<p>You don’t need to be technical. Most of these steps just take minutes—and they’ll make a huge difference when 5.0 goes live.</p>



<p>Complexity Key: Each task includes a quick complexity rating:<br><br><img src="https://s.w.org/images/core/emoji/16.0.1/72x72/1f7e2.png" alt="🟢" class="wp-smiley" style="height: 1em; max-height: 1em;" /> Easy: These are quick tasks you should be able to do.&nbsp;</p>



<p><img src="https://s.w.org/images/core/emoji/16.0.1/72x72/1f7e1.png" alt="🟡" class="wp-smiley" style="height: 1em; max-height: 1em;" /> Moderate: These may require some additional familiarity or a plugin.&nbsp;</p>



<p><img src="https://s.w.org/images/core/emoji/16.0.1/72x72/1f534.png" alt="🔴" class="wp-smiley" style="height: 1em; max-height: 1em;" /> Advanced: These tasks could require developer assistance.&nbsp;</p>



<h3 class="wp-block-heading" id="h-steps-to-take-now-before-learndash-5-0-is-released">Steps to Take Now — <em>Before LearnDash 5.0 Is Released</em></h3>



<p>These steps help you prepare your site early, so you’re not scrambling on release day.</p>



<div class="wp-block-kadence-accordion alignnone"><div class="kt-accordion-wrap kt-accordion-id27168_938434-f1 kt-accordion-has-6-panes kt-active-pane-0 kt-accordion-block kt-pane-header-alignment-left kt-accodion-icon-style-basic kt-accodion-icon-side-right" style="max-width:none"><div class="kt-accordion-inner-wrap" data-allow-multiple-open="false" data-start-open="none">
<div class="wp-block-kadence-pane kt-accordion-pane kt-accordion-pane-1 kt-pane27168_7afca5-95"><div class="kt-accordion-header-wrap"><button class="kt-blocks-accordion-header kt-acccordion-button-label-show" type="button"><span class="kt-blocks-accordion-title-wrap"><span class="kt-blocks-accordion-title">1. Make a Fresh Backup</span></span><span class="kt-blocks-accordion-icon-trigger"></span></button></div><div class="kt-accordion-panel kt-accordion-panel-hidden"><div class="kt-accordion-panel-inner">
<p><strong>What to do:</strong><strong><br></strong>Ensure you have a current backup of your entire site, including files and database.</p>



<p><strong>How:</strong></p>



<ul class="wp-block-list">
<li>Many hosting providers offer automatic backups—confirm that yours is recent.</li>



<li>If not, use a plugin like SolidWP to back up your site.<br></li>
</ul>



<p><strong>Why it matters:</strong><br>A current backup is your safety net. If anything goes wrong, you can restore your site quickly.<br><br><strong>Complexity</strong>: <img src="https://s.w.org/images/core/emoji/16.0.1/72x72/1f7e2.png" alt="🟢" class="wp-smiley" style="height: 1em; max-height: 1em;" /> Easy</p>
</div></div></div>



<div class="wp-block-kadence-pane kt-accordion-pane kt-accordion-pane-2 kt-pane27168_7e95bc-6d"><div class="kt-accordion-header-wrap"><button class="kt-blocks-accordion-header kt-acccordion-button-label-show" type="button"><span class="kt-blocks-accordion-title-wrap"><span class="kt-blocks-accordion-title">2. List Your Add-Ons and Integrations</span></span><span class="kt-blocks-accordion-icon-trigger"></span></button></div><div class="kt-accordion-panel kt-accordion-panel-hidden"><div class="kt-accordion-panel-inner">
<p><strong>What to do:</strong><strong><br></strong>Create a list of every LearnDash-related plugin or integration you’re using.</p>



<p><strong>Examples:</strong></p>



<ul class="wp-block-list">
<li>Official LearnDash add-ons (e.g., Certificates, Groups, Assignments, etc.)</li>



<li>Third-party plugins (e.g., Uncanny Automator, MemberPress, WP Fusion, etc.)</li>



<li>Any custom reporting, dashboards, or automations<br></li>
</ul>



<p><strong>Why it matters:</strong><br>Having a clear list helps you quickly verify compatibility after the update.<br></p>



<p><strong>Complexity</strong>: <img src="https://s.w.org/images/core/emoji/16.0.1/72x72/1f7e2.png" alt="🟢" class="wp-smiley" style="height: 1em; max-height: 1em;" /> Easy</p>
</div></div></div>



<div class="wp-block-kadence-pane kt-accordion-pane kt-accordion-pane-3 kt-pane27168_eef298-5c"><div class="kt-accordion-header-wrap"><button class="kt-blocks-accordion-header kt-acccordion-button-label-show" type="button"><span class="kt-blocks-accordion-title-wrap"><span class="kt-blocks-accordion-title">3. Check for Available Updates</span></span><span class="kt-blocks-accordion-icon-trigger"></span></button></div><div class="kt-accordion-panel kt-accordion-panel-hidden"><div class="kt-accordion-panel-inner">
<p><strong>What to do:</strong><br>Update everything else now—themes, plugins, and WordPress itself.</p>



<p><strong>Why it matters:</strong><br>Many compatibility issues come from outdated software, not the new release itself.</p>



<p><strong>Complexity</strong>: <img src="https://s.w.org/images/core/emoji/16.0.1/72x72/1f7e2.png" alt="🟢" class="wp-smiley" style="height: 1em; max-height: 1em;" /> Easy</p>
</div></div></div>



<div class="wp-block-kadence-pane kt-accordion-pane kt-accordion-pane-4 kt-pane27168_5db826-6f"><div class="kt-accordion-header-wrap"><button class="kt-blocks-accordion-header kt-acccordion-button-label-show" type="button"><span class="kt-blocks-accordion-title-wrap"><span class="kt-blocks-accordion-title">4. Set Up a Staging Site</span></span><span class="kt-blocks-accordion-icon-trigger"></span></button></div><div class="kt-accordion-panel kt-accordion-panel-hidden"><div class="kt-accordion-panel-inner">
<p><strong>What to do:</strong><br>Create a staging version of your site to test LearnDash 5.0 safely before going live.&nbsp;</p>



<p><strong>How:</strong></p>



<ul class="wp-block-list">
<li>Ask your hosting provider if they offer staging.</li>



<li>Or use a plugin like WP Staging to create one yourself.<br></li>
</ul>



<p><strong>Why it matters:</strong><strong><br></strong>You’ll be ready to test 5.0 as soon as it’s available, with zero risk to your live site.</p>



<p><strong>Complexity</strong>: <img src="https://s.w.org/images/core/emoji/16.0.1/72x72/1f7e1.png" alt="🟡" class="wp-smiley" style="height: 1em; max-height: 1em;" /> Moderate</p>
</div></div></div>



<div class="wp-block-kadence-pane kt-accordion-pane kt-accordion-pane-5 kt-pane27168_1ca42b-a8"><div class="kt-accordion-header-wrap"><button class="kt-blocks-accordion-header kt-acccordion-button-label-show" type="button"><span class="kt-blocks-accordion-title-wrap"><span class="kt-blocks-accordion-title">5. Identify Custom Code or Snippets</span></span><span class="kt-blocks-accordion-icon-trigger"></span></button></div><div class="kt-accordion-panel kt-accordion-panel-hidden"><div class="kt-accordion-panel-inner">
<p><strong>What to do:</strong><br>Check if your site uses any custom LearnDash-related code, especially functions that display course progress, quiz data, or custom reports.</p>



<p><strong>How:</strong><strong><br></strong>Look in your <strong>functions.php</strong> file or a plugin like “Code Snippets.”</p>



<p><strong>Why it matters:</strong><br>LearnDash 5.0 includes updated REST API field names (e.g.,<strong> in_progress</strong> replaces <strong>inProgress</strong>), so custom code may require minor updates.<br></p>



<p><strong>Complexity</strong>: <img src="https://s.w.org/images/core/emoji/16.0.1/72x72/1f534.png" alt="🔴" class="wp-smiley" style="height: 1em; max-height: 1em;" /> Advanced&nbsp;</p>
</div></div></div>



<div class="wp-block-kadence-pane kt-accordion-pane kt-accordion-pane-6 kt-pane27168_b4a895-17"><div class="kt-accordion-header-wrap"><button class="kt-blocks-accordion-header kt-acccordion-button-label-show" type="button"><span class="kt-blocks-accordion-title-wrap"><span class="kt-blocks-accordion-title">6. Monitor LearnDash Communications </span></span><span class="kt-blocks-accordion-icon-trigger"></span></button></div><div class="kt-accordion-panel kt-accordion-panel-hidden"><div class="kt-accordion-panel-inner">
<p><strong>What to do:</strong><br>Stay subscribed to the LearnDash newsletter and keep an eye on blog announcements.</p>



<p><strong>Why it matters:</strong><br>We’ll share the release date, testing updates, and developer notes leading up to 5.0 and afterwards.</p>



<p><strong>Complexity</strong>: <img src="https://s.w.org/images/core/emoji/16.0.1/72x72/1f7e2.png" alt="🟢" class="wp-smiley" style="height: 1em; max-height: 1em;" /> Easy</p>
</div></div></div>
</div></div></div>



<h3 class="wp-block-heading" id="h-steps-to-take-right-before-updating-to-learndash-5-0">Steps to Take Right Before Updating to LearnDash 5.0</h3>



<p>Once LearnDash 5.0 is released—or you’re ready to install it on staging—follow these steps to make sure everything runs smoothly.</p>



<div class="wp-block-kadence-accordion alignnone"><div class="kt-accordion-wrap kt-accordion-id27168_47b3c1-ba kt-accordion-has-7-panes kt-active-pane-0 kt-accordion-block kt-pane-header-alignment-left kt-accodion-icon-style-basic kt-accodion-icon-side-right" style="max-width:none"><div class="kt-accordion-inner-wrap" data-allow-multiple-open="false" data-start-open="none">
<div class="wp-block-kadence-pane kt-accordion-pane kt-accordion-pane-1 kt-pane27168_79a07d-65"><div class="kt-accordion-header-wrap"><button class="kt-blocks-accordion-header kt-acccordion-button-label-show" type="button"><span class="kt-blocks-accordion-title-wrap"><span class="kt-blocks-accordion-title">1. Confirm You Have a Backup and Staging Site</span></span><span class="kt-blocks-accordion-icon-trigger"></span></button></div><div class="kt-accordion-panel kt-accordion-panel-hidden"><div class="kt-accordion-panel-inner">
<p><strong>What to do:</strong></p>



<p>Make sure both are set up and ready to go with your most recent backup.</p>



<p><strong>Why it matters:</strong><br>You’ll want a fallback option if anything needs troubleshooting post-update.</p>



<p><strong>Complexity</strong>: <img src="https://s.w.org/images/core/emoji/16.0.1/72x72/1f7e2.png" alt="🟢" class="wp-smiley" style="height: 1em; max-height: 1em;" /> Easy</p>
</div></div></div>



<div class="wp-block-kadence-pane kt-accordion-pane kt-accordion-pane-2 kt-pane27168_c7ba69-b3"><div class="kt-accordion-header-wrap"><button class="kt-blocks-accordion-header kt-acccordion-button-label-show" type="button"><span class="kt-blocks-accordion-title-wrap"><span class="kt-blocks-accordion-title">2. Update Add-Ons and Integrations First</span></span><span class="kt-blocks-accordion-icon-trigger"></span></button></div><div class="kt-accordion-panel kt-accordion-panel-hidden"><div class="kt-accordion-panel-inner">
<p><strong>What to do:</strong><br>Update all plugins that connect to LearnDash. Many developers are releasing 5.0 compatibility updates.</p>



<p><strong>How:</strong></p>



<ul class="wp-block-list">
<li>Visit each plugin’s settings page or WordPress.org listing.</li>



<li>Check for version notes referencing LearnDash 5.0.<br></li>
</ul>



<p><strong>Why it matters:</strong><br>Outdated add-ons cause the most compatibility issues.</p>



<p><strong>Complexity</strong>: <img src="https://s.w.org/images/core/emoji/16.0.1/72x72/1f7e1.png" alt="🟡" class="wp-smiley" style="height: 1em; max-height: 1em;" /> Moderate</p>
</div></div></div>



<div class="wp-block-kadence-pane kt-accordion-pane kt-accordion-pane-3 kt-pane27168_a06482-27"><div class="kt-accordion-header-wrap"><button class="kt-blocks-accordion-header kt-acccordion-button-label-show" type="button"><span class="kt-blocks-accordion-title-wrap"><span class="kt-blocks-accordion-title">3. Test Course Progress and Quizzes</span></span><span class="kt-blocks-accordion-icon-trigger"></span></button></div><div class="kt-accordion-panel kt-accordion-panel-hidden"><div class="kt-accordion-panel-inner">
<p><strong>What to do:</strong><br>Log in as a test student and complete a few lessons and quizzes.&nbsp;</p>



<p><strong>What to check:</strong></p>



<ul class="wp-block-list">
<li>Lesson completion</li>



<li>Quiz scoring and certificate generation</li>



<li>Course progress tracking<br></li>
</ul>



<p><strong>Why it matters:</strong><br>These are all powered by the REST API. Testing ensures they are functioning correctly.<br><br><strong>Complexity</strong>: <img src="https://s.w.org/images/core/emoji/16.0.1/72x72/1f7e2.png" alt="🟢" class="wp-smiley" style="height: 1em; max-height: 1em;" /> Easy</p>
</div></div></div>



<div class="wp-block-kadence-pane kt-accordion-pane kt-accordion-pane-4 kt-pane27168_23843f-89"><div class="kt-accordion-header-wrap"><button class="kt-blocks-accordion-header kt-acccordion-button-label-show" type="button"><span class="kt-blocks-accordion-title-wrap"><span class="kt-blocks-accordion-title">4. Check Automations and Reporting Tools</span></span><span class="kt-blocks-accordion-icon-trigger"></span></button></div><div class="kt-accordion-panel kt-accordion-panel-hidden"><div class="kt-accordion-panel-inner">
<p><strong>What to do:</strong><br>Test any automations (e.g., Zapier, Uncanny Automator) or custom reporting tools.&nbsp;</p>



<p><strong>Why it matters:</strong><br>These tools may rely on the API. If they don’t trigger or display correctly, they may need updates.</p>



<p><strong>Complexity</strong>: <img src="https://s.w.org/images/core/emoji/16.0.1/72x72/1f7e1.png" alt="🟡" class="wp-smiley" style="height: 1em; max-height: 1em;" /> Moderate</p>
</div></div></div>



<div class="wp-block-kadence-pane kt-accordion-pane kt-accordion-pane-5 kt-pane27168_f0d594-31"><div class="kt-accordion-header-wrap"><button class="kt-blocks-accordion-header kt-acccordion-button-label-show" type="button"><span class="kt-blocks-accordion-title-wrap"><span class="kt-blocks-accordion-title">5. Clear Site and Browser Cache</span></span><span class="kt-blocks-accordion-icon-trigger"></span></button></div><div class="kt-accordion-panel kt-accordion-panel-hidden"><div class="kt-accordion-panel-inner">
<p><strong>What to do:</strong><strong><br></strong>After updating, clear your site cache and browser cache.</p>



<p><strong>Why it matters:</strong><br>Old cached files can cause display issues or hide the latest data.<br><br><strong>Complexity</strong>: <img src="https://s.w.org/images/core/emoji/16.0.1/72x72/1f7e2.png" alt="🟢" class="wp-smiley" style="height: 1em; max-height: 1em;" /> Easy</p>
</div></div></div>



<div class="wp-block-kadence-pane kt-accordion-pane kt-accordion-pane-6 kt-pane27168_638a9d-9a"><div class="kt-accordion-header-wrap"><button class="kt-blocks-accordion-header kt-acccordion-button-label-show" type="button"><span class="kt-blocks-accordion-title-wrap"><span class="kt-blocks-accordion-title">6. Review Key Workflows on Live Site</span></span><span class="kt-blocks-accordion-icon-trigger"></span></button></div><div class="kt-accordion-panel kt-accordion-panel-hidden"><div class="kt-accordion-panel-inner">
<p><strong>What to do:</strong><br>After successful testing on staging, update your live site and run through typical user workflows.&nbsp;</p>



<p><strong>Why it matters</strong>:<br>Confirms that everything works smoothly in your production environment.</p>



<p><strong>Complexity</strong>: <img src="https://s.w.org/images/core/emoji/16.0.1/72x72/1f7e2.png" alt="🟢" class="wp-smiley" style="height: 1em; max-height: 1em;" /> Easy</p>
</div></div></div>



<div class="wp-block-kadence-pane kt-accordion-pane kt-accordion-pane-7 kt-pane27168_06825e-fb"><div class="kt-accordion-header-wrap"><button class="kt-blocks-accordion-header kt-acccordion-button-label-show" type="button"><span class="kt-blocks-accordion-title-wrap"><span class="kt-blocks-accordion-title">7. Stay Updated Post-Launch</span></span><span class="kt-blocks-accordion-icon-trigger"></span></button></div><div class="kt-accordion-panel kt-accordion-panel-hidden"><div class="kt-accordion-panel-inner">
<p><strong>What to do:</strong><br>Keep an eye on LearnDash announcements for any post-release notes or refinements.</p>



<p><strong>Why it matters:</strong><br>We’ll be closely monitoring early feedback to ensure smooth adoption across all sites.</p>



<p><strong>Complexity</strong>: <img src="https://s.w.org/images/core/emoji/16.0.1/72x72/1f7e2.png" alt="🟢" class="wp-smiley" style="height: 1em; max-height: 1em;" /> Easy</p>
</div></div></div>
</div></div></div>



<h2 class="wp-block-heading" id="h-why-all-this-preparation-matters">Why All This Preparation Matters</h2>



<p>We know this looks like a lot—but it’s how we ensure LearnDash 5.0 benefits every user.&nbsp;</p>



<p>This update is designed to remove friction, not add it. With a modern, streamlined codebase, LearnDash 5.0 delivers what creators have been asking for:&nbsp;</p>



<ul class="wp-block-list">
<li>Faster performance and better reliability</li>



<li>Seamless integration with third-party tools and add-ons</li>



<li>A foundation for future AI-assisted features and improved reporting</li>



<li>New features and enhanced functionality delivered quicker&nbsp;</li>



<li>Unblocking legacy bug fixes</li>
</ul>



<p>Preparation today ensures your LearnDash site won’t just survive the update, it’ll thrive because of it.</p>



<h2 class="wp-block-heading" id="h-need-help-before-or-after-the-update">Need Help Before or After the Update?</h2>



<p>If you’re not sure how to do something here:</p>



<ul class="wp-block-list">
<li>Ask your hosting provider about staging or backups.</li>



<li>Contact your developer if you use custom code.</li>



<li>Or visit our <a href="https://www.learndash.com/support/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">Knowledge Base</a> for additional LearnDash documentation.</li>
</ul>



<h2 class="wp-block-heading" id="h-final-thoughts">Final Thoughts</h2>



<p>LearnDash 5.0 marks a major leap forward.</p>



<p>It introduces the technical foundation for a new generation of LMS features: AI-assisted course building, advanced analytics, visual learning paths, and smarter student management tools.</p>



<p>A few simple steps today will make update day smooth, and your LMS stronger for years to come.</p>



<p>Let’s move learning forward—together.</p>



<p></p>
