			";s:7:"attribs";a:0:{}s:8:"xml_base";s:0:"";s:17:"xml_base_explicit";b:0;s:8:"xml_lang";s:0:"";s:5:"child";a:3:{s:0:"";a:6:{s:5:"title";a:1:{i:0;a:5:{s:4:"data";s:33:"Featured Customer: Brandy Stoffel";s:7:"attribs";a:0:{}s:8:"xml_base";s:0:"";s:17:"xml_base_explicit";b:0;s:8:"xml_lang";s:0:"";}}s:4:"link";a:1:{i:0;a:5:{s:4:"data";s:66:"https://www.learndash.com/blog/ai-powered-essay-grading-learndash/";s:7:"attribs";a:0:{}s:8:"xml_base";s:0:"";s:17:"xml_base_explicit";b:0;s:8:"xml_lang";s:0:"";}}s:7:"pubDate";a:1:{i:0;a:5:{s:4:"data";s:31:"Thu, 14 Aug 2025 15:10:33 +0000";s:7:"attribs";a:0:{}s:8:"xml_base";s:0:"";s:17:"xml_base_explicit";b:0;s:8:"xml_lang";s:0:"";}}s:8:"category";a:1:{i:0;a:5:{s:4:"data";s:17:"Customer Showcase";s:7:"attribs";a:0:{}s:8:"xml_base";s:0:"";s:17:"xml_base_explicit";b:0;s:8:"xml_lang";s:0:"";}}s:4:"guid";a:1:{i:0;a:5:{s:4:"data";s:34:"https://www.learndash.com/?p=25753";s:7:"attribs";a:1:{s:0:"";a:1:{s:11:"isPermaLink";s:5:"false";}}s:8:"xml_base";s:0:"";s:17:"xml_base_explicit";b:0;s:8:"xml_lang";s:0:"";}}s:11:"description";a:1:{i:0;a:5:{s:4:"data";s:205:"Nursing educator Brandy Stoffel created AI Gr-Aid, a LearnDash-compatible plugin that grades factual essay questions with AI-powered accuracy, provides personalized feedback, and saves her 20 hours a week.";s:7:"attribs";a:0:{}s:8:"xml_base";s:0:"";s:17:"xml_base_explicit";b:0;s:8:"xml_lang";s:0:"";}}}s:32:"http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/";a:1:{s:7:"creator";a:1:{i:0;a:5:{s:4:"data";s:17:"Jaime Marchwinski";s:7:"attribs";a:0:{}s:8:"xml_base";s:0:"";s:17:"xml_base_explicit";b:0;s:8:"xml_lang";s:0:"";}}}s:40:"http://purl.org/rss/1.0/modules/content/";a:1:{s:7:"encoded";a:1:{i:0;a:5:{s:4:"data";s:6525:"
<p>When it comes to nursing education, <em>understanding</em> matters far more than guessing the right multiple-choice option. For Oregon-based nurse educator <strong>Brandy Stoffel</strong>, that meant finding a way to truly assess her students’ knowledge — while also managing the enormous time burden that grading factual essay responses creates.</p>



<p>Instead of compromising, Brandy built a custom solution: <strong>AI Gr-Aid</strong> — an AI-powered grading assistant that integrates seamlessly with <a href="https://www.learndash.com/learndash-lms/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">LearnDash for educators</a> and WordPress to deliver precise, constructive feedback on every student’s essay.</p>



<hr class="wp-block-separator has-alpha-channel-opacity"/>



<h3 class="wp-block-heading" id="h-the-challenge-essays-without-the-overwhelm"><strong>The Challenge: Essays Without the Overwhelm</strong></h3>



<p>Brandy runs a <a href="https://nursereentry.com/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">Nurse Re-Entry Program</a> in Oregon, where her students must demonstrate clinical knowledge through factual essay questions. This isn’t about creative writing or opinions — it’s about proving competence with correct, precise answers.</p>



<p>The problem?<br>Manual grading took <em>hours</em>. For Brandy, that meant spending 20+ hours a week reading, scoring, and writing individual feedback for each student.</p>



<p>And while <a href="https://www.learndash.com/blog/tips-for-writing-smarter-e-learning-quizzes/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">LearnDash’s advanced quiz and assessment features</a> worked for quizzes and multiple-choice questions, there was no built-in way to grade factual essays with the level of specificity she needed.</p>



<hr class="wp-block-separator has-alpha-channel-opacity"/>



<h3 class="wp-block-heading" id="h-the-solution-ai-gr-aid"><strong>The Solution: AI Gr-Aid</strong></h3>



<p>Brandy worked with developers to create <strong>AI Gr-Aid</strong>, a custom LearnDash-compatible plugin that puts <em>instructors</em> in control of the grading process.</p>



<p>Here’s how it works:</p>



<ul class="wp-block-list">
<li><strong>You set the “correct” answer</strong> for each essay question.</li>



<li>Students submit their responses through LearnDash.</li>



<li>The AI compares the student’s answer against your defined correct answer — not its own assumptions.</li>



<li>Every student gets <strong>specific, tailored feedback</strong> on their answer, even if they pass.</li>
</ul>



<p>It’s not a generic AI summary — the feedback is unique to the student’s actual submission.</p>



<p><strong>Inside the “Submitted Essays” admin panel</strong>, instructors see:</p>



<ul class="wp-block-list">
<li>The student’s answer alongside the “correct” answer</li>



<li>Pass/fail status</li>



<li>Points awarded</li>



<li>A concise feedback summary with improvement suggestions</li>
</ul>



<p>For students, the experience is simple: they see their response, the points earned, and constructive notes on how to improve.</p>



<hr class="wp-block-separator has-alpha-channel-opacity"/>



<h3 class="wp-block-heading" id="h-why-it-works"><strong>Why It Works</strong></h3>



<ul class="wp-block-list">
<li><strong>Accuracy Control</strong> – Instructors can set a sensitivity threshold (typically 70–80%) to define how closely a student’s answer must match.</li>



<li><strong>Multilingual Capability</strong> – Tested in French and Spanish, it works just as smoothly as in English, making it perfect for <a href="https://learndash.com/support/kb/resources/user-guides/translation/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">multilingual course delivery</a>.</li>



<li><strong>Time Savings</strong> – Brandy now saves about <strong>20 hours every week</strong> on grading — without sacrificing quality.</li>



<li><strong>Instructor Authority</strong> – AI evaluates based on <em>your</em> standards, not a general AI model’s knowledge.</li>
</ul>



<blockquote class="wp-block-quote is-layout-flow wp-block-quote-is-layout-flow">
<p>“The tool gives me back my time without taking away my control as an educator,” Brandy says. “Every student still gets feedback, and I know it’s aligned with exactly what I’m looking for.”</p>
</blockquote>



<p>For educators who want to <a href="https://www.learndash.com/blog/feedback-loops-in-online-learning/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">improve learner engagement with feedback</a>, this model is a game-changer.</p>



<hr class="wp-block-separator has-alpha-channel-opacity"/>



<h3 class="wp-block-heading" id="h-a-better-ai-for-learndash"><strong>A Better AI for LearnDash</strong></h3>



<p>While Brandy values AI as a grading assistant, she’s not a fan of current AI chatbots that pull from the entire internet.</p>



<p>Her vision? <strong>Course-aware AI</strong> — an assistant that only references <em>your</em> LearnDash course content, ensuring students get accurate, context-specific support. AI Gr-Aid already embodies that principle by grading solely against instructor-defined answers.</p>



<p>If you’re curious about using AI in online learning, Brandy’s approach shows how it can be implemented with precision and purpose.</p>



<hr class="wp-block-separator has-alpha-channel-opacity"/>



<h3 class="wp-block-heading" id="h-the-future-from-custom-tool-to-community-benefit"><strong>The Future: From Custom Tool to Community Benefit</strong></h3>



<p>Brandy isn’t trying to launch a tech startup — she simply built AI Gr-Aid to solve her own grading problem. But she believes the tool could benefit countless other educators using LearnDash.</p>



<blockquote class="wp-block-quote is-layout-flow wp-block-quote-is-layout-flow">
<p>“I’d love to see LearnDash integrate AI Gr-Aid so other instructors can reclaim their time without losing the depth and accuracy of essay-based assessment.”</p>
</blockquote>



<p>If you want to <a href="https://www.learndash.com/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">get started with LearnDash today</a> or <a href="https://demo.learndash.com/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">try out the LearnDash demo</a>, Brandy’s story proves what’s possible when innovative educators pair teaching expertise with the right technology.</p>



<hr class="wp-block-separator has-alpha-channel-opacity"/>



<p></p>
