			";s:7:"attribs";a:0:{}s:8:"xml_base";s:0:"";s:17:"xml_base_explicit";b:0;s:8:"xml_lang";s:0:"";s:5:"child";a:3:{s:0:"";a:6:{s:5:"title";a:1:{i:0;a:5:{s:4:"data";s:29:"Featured Customer: StringKick";s:7:"attribs";a:0:{}s:8:"xml_base";s:0:"";s:17:"xml_base_explicit";b:0;s:8:"xml_lang";s:0:"";}}s:4:"link";a:1:{i:0;a:5:{s:4:"data";s:61:"https://www.learndash.com/blog/featured-customer-string-kick/";s:7:"attribs";a:0:{}s:8:"xml_base";s:0:"";s:17:"xml_base_explicit";b:0;s:8:"xml_lang";s:0:"";}}s:7:"pubDate";a:1:{i:0;a:5:{s:4:"data";s:31:"Wed, 02 Jul 2025 13:52:51 +0000";s:7:"attribs";a:0:{}s:8:"xml_base";s:0:"";s:17:"xml_base_explicit";b:0;s:8:"xml_lang";s:0:"";}}s:8:"category";a:1:{i:0;a:5:{s:4:"data";s:17:"Customer Showcase";s:7:"attribs";a:0:{}s:8:"xml_base";s:0:"";s:17:"xml_base_explicit";b:0;s:8:"xml_lang";s:0:"";}}s:4:"guid";a:1:{i:0;a:5:{s:4:"data";s:34:"https://www.learndash.com/?p=24998";s:7:"attribs";a:1:{s:0:"";a:1:{s:11:"isPermaLink";s:5:"false";}}s:8:"xml_base";s:0:"";s:17:"xml_base_explicit";b:0;s:8:"xml_lang";s:0:"";}}s:11:"description";a:1:{i:0;a:5:{s:4:"data";s:306:"From guitar teacher to founder of a thriving e-learning platform, Just Rijna built StringKick with LearnDash to give musicians a smarter way to train their ears. Discover how he turned a side project into a full-time business with custom ear-training tools, gamified learning, and a reliable WordPress LMS.";s:7:"attribs";a:0:{}s:8:"xml_base";s:0:"";s:17:"xml_base_explicit";b:0;s:8:"xml_lang";s:0:"";}}}s:32:"http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/";a:1:{s:7:"creator";a:1:{i:0;a:5:{s:4:"data";s:17:"Jaime Marchwinski";s:7:"attribs";a:0:{}s:8:"xml_base";s:0:"";s:17:"xml_base_explicit";b:0;s:8:"xml_lang";s:0:"";}}}s:40:"http://purl.org/rss/1.0/modules/content/";a:1:{s:7:"encoded";a:1:{i:0;a:5:{s:4:"data";s:7252:"
<h4 class="wp-block-heading" id="h-from-in-person-lessons-to-a-thriving-online-platform"><strong>From In-Person Lessons to a Thriving Online Platform</strong></h4>



<p>Just Rijna, the creator of<a href="https://www.stringkick.com" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener"> StringKick</a>, started as an in-person guitar teacher before transitioning to online courses. He wanted to teach musicians how to train their ears, recognize chords, and develop musical intuition—not just follow sheet music. But finding the right platform to bring his vision to life was a challenge.</p>



<h4 class="wp-block-heading" id="h-choosing-learndash-over-saas-platforms"><strong>Choosing LearnDash Over SaaS Platforms</strong></h4>



<p>Before settling on <a href="https://www.learndash.com/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">LearnDash</a>, Just explored platforms like Udemy and Teachable. However, these SaaS solutions came with limitations that didn&#8217;t align with his long-term vision.</p>



<blockquote class="wp-block-quote is-layout-flow wp-block-quote-is-layout-flow">
<p>“If I build on SaaS, I’m building on borrowed land.”</p>
</blockquote>



<p>Not owning his customer list and not having control over his content was a dealbreaker. He needed a flexible, customizable platform that integrates seamlessly with his website. WordPress was the obvious choice for him, and LearnDash was one of the first plugins he picked—one that has powered his courses for the last nine years.</p>



<h4 class="wp-block-heading" id="h-turning-an-experiment-into-a-full-time-business"><strong>Turning an Experiment into a Full-Time Business</strong></h4>



<p>What started as a small project has grown into a full-time career. StringKick now attracts tens of thousands of monthly visitors, and students have completed over 100,000 LearnDash lessons.</p>



<p>Just built a custom ear-training module within LearnDash that allows students to listen to a song, chord, or riff and interactively identify what they hear. This unique approach helps musicians internalize music in the same way they would learn a language.</p>



<figure class="wp-block-image size-full"><img decoding="async" src="https://www.learndash.com/wp-content/uploads/Image-4.png" alt="" class="wp-image-25045"/></figure>



<h4 class="wp-block-heading" id="h-a-streamlined-learning-experience-with-gamification-amp-automation"><strong>A Streamlined Learning Experience with Gamification &amp; Automation</strong></h4>



<p>To keep students engaged, StringKick uses GamiPress to track progress and achievements. Students earn experience points for each lesson completed, and key milestones trigger pop-up achievements—small but effective reminders of their progress.</p>



<figure class="wp-block-image size-full"><img decoding="async" src="https://www.learndash.com/wp-content/uploads/Image-1-1.png" alt="" class="wp-image-25046"/></figure>



<p>Additionally, Just leverages WP Fusion to manage course access based on membership levels. Initially, he sold courses individually, but later transitioned to an All Access membership model with monthly and annual plans.</p>



<blockquote class="wp-block-quote is-layout-flow wp-block-quote-is-layout-flow">
<p>“With enough persistence and grit, you can make anything happen.”</p>
</blockquote>



<figure class="wp-block-kadence-image kb-image24998_1a4ad6-a3 size-large"><picture fetchpriority="high" decoding="async" class="kb-img wp-image-27350">
<source type="image/webp" srcset="https://www.learndash.com/wp-content/uploads/Learning-Path-Larger-785x1024.jpg.webp 785w, https://www.learndash.com/wp-content/uploads/Learning-Path-Larger-230x300.jpg.webp 230w, https://www.learndash.com/wp-content/uploads/Learning-Path-Larger-768x1002.jpg.webp 768w, https://www.learndash.com/wp-content/uploads/Learning-Path-Larger-1177x1536.jpg.webp 1177w, https://www.learndash.com/wp-content/uploads/Learning-Path-Larger.jpg.webp 828w" sizes="(max-width: 785px) 100vw, 785px"/>
<img fetchpriority="high" decoding="async" width="785" height="1024" src="https://www.learndash.com/wp-content/uploads/Learning-Path-Larger-785x1024.jpg" alt="" class="kb-img wp-image-27350" srcset="https://www.learndash.com/wp-content/uploads/Learning-Path-Larger-785x1024.jpg 785w, https://www.learndash.com/wp-content/uploads/Learning-Path-Larger-230x300.jpg 230w, https://www.learndash.com/wp-content/uploads/Learning-Path-Larger-768x1002.jpg 768w, https://www.learndash.com/wp-content/uploads/Learning-Path-Larger-1177x1536.jpg 1177w, https://www.learndash.com/wp-content/uploads/Learning-Path-Larger.jpg 828w" sizes="(max-width: 785px) 100vw, 785px"/>
</picture>
</figure>



<p>Just&#8217;s latest development is <a href="https://www.stringkick.com/guitar-games/">StringKick Games</a>: a Duolingo-like set of interactive, gamified exercises that help guitarists with fretboard fluency, ear training and music theory. It features a custom &#8220;learning path&#8221; interface that visualises progress through levels and sections, showing how flexible LearnDash can be with a bit of creativity.</p>



<h4 class="wp-block-heading" id="h-a-lean-amp-reliable-system"><strong>A Lean &amp; Reliable System</strong></h4>



<p>Just values reliability above all. He runs a lean and clean system, only keeping plugins that work seamlessly together.</p>



<blockquote class="wp-block-quote is-layout-flow wp-block-quote-is-layout-flow">
<p>“When plugins break things, I stop using them. When I click the update button, I trust it won’t break things.”</p>
</blockquote>



<p>LearnDash has consistently met his needs, working reliably without requiring constant attention. His favorite part of running StringKick? Hearing from students who say his courses have completely changed how they experience music.</p>



<figure class="wp-block-image size-full"><img decoding="async" src="https://www.learndash.com/wp-content/uploads/Image-2-1.png" alt="" class="wp-image-25049"/></figure>



<h4 class="wp-block-heading" id="h-advice-for-those-considering-learndash"><strong>Advice for Those Considering LearnDash</strong></h4>



<p>For anyone on the fence about LearnDash, Just’s advice is simple:</p>



<blockquote class="wp-block-quote is-layout-flow wp-block-quote-is-layout-flow">
<p>&#8220;It’s the go-to solution for a WordPress LMS. It’s been reliable for me for nine years, and it integrates easily with other key plugins like WooCommerce, WP Fusion, and GamiPress.&#8221;</p>
</blockquote>



<figure class="wp-block-image size-full"><img decoding="async" src="https://www.learndash.com/wp-content/uploads/Image-3.png" alt="" class="wp-image-25047"/></figure>



<h3 class="wp-block-heading" id="h-explore-stringkick"><strong>Explore StringKick</strong></h3>



<p>Just&#8217;s courses are designed for a wide range of musicians, from beginners to professionals looking to sharpen their ear training. If you&#8217;re curious, check out his in-depth guide on<a href="https://www.stringkick.com/blog-lessons/guitar-music-theory/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener"> guitar music theory</a> or explore the<a href="https://www.stringkick.com/join/#enroll" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener"> All Access membership</a>.</p>
